00:13:37,700 --> 00:13:38,980
It's taking over Melchior!

271
00:13:39,280 --> 00:13:40,680
And it's hacking into Balthazar!

272
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:43,480
Fast!

273
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,340
Too fast!

274
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:47,900
It's calculation speed.

275
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:48,480
It's incredible!

276
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,800
Change the login mode!

277
00:13:57,960 --> 00:14:00,460
Change synchronization code to every 15 seconds!

278
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:00,840
Roger!

279
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:01,380
Yes, ma'am!

280
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:08,580
How much time did we buy?

281
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:10,160
At least two hours.

282
00:14:10,860 --> 00:14:11,420
I think.

283
00:14:12,200 --> 00:14:15,160
The Magi have become our enemy.

284
00:14:15,160 --> 00:14:26,780
This Angel must be composed of a group of nanomachines, each the size of a virus.

285
00:14:27,380 --> 00:14:31,380
These nanomachines then group together to form colonies, and in a very short period of

286
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:36,700
time, they mutate in a focused exponential series to form a sophisticated intelligent circuit.

287
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:37,460
Evolution.

288
00:14:37,820 --> 00:14:38,120
Yes.

289
00:14:38,400 --> 00:14:42,500
They're continuously changing and adapting themselves to attain the best system to cope

290
00:14:42,500 --> 00:14:44,260
with any environment they may encounter.

291
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:45,320
I understand.

292
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:47,820
It's this Angel's survival mechanism.

293
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:48,940
Total adaptability.

294
00:14:49,160 --> 00:14:53,280
The only effective countermeasure for an enemy that continually evolves to overcome

295
00:14:53,280 --> 00:14:55,440
its own weakness is to eliminate the host.

296
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:58,440
If the Magi died, the parasites died too.

297
00:14:58,600 --> 00:15:01,560
Therefore, Commander, I propose the physical destruction of the Magi.

298
00:15:01,660 --> 00:15:02,120
Impossible!

299
00:15:02,560 --> 00:15:05,320
Destroying the Magi means destroying headquarters itself.

300
00:15:05,460 --> 00:15:08,020
That's my recommendation as head of operations!

301
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:09,080
You're out of line!

302
00:15:09,260 --> 00:15:11,740
This situation is the responsibility of my department.

303
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:13,380
Why are you being so stubborn?

304
00:15:13,380 --> 00:15:16,880
This whole thing is a result of my carelessness.

305
00:15:18,600 --> 00:15:20,520
Why do you have to be like this?

306
00:15:20,820 --> 00:15:22,320
You never share the responsibility.

307
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:25,680
Why won't you trust someone else?

308
00:15:25,680 --> 00:15:31,040
As long as this Angel keeps evolving, we still have a chance.

309
00:15:31,180 --> 00:15:32,760
By controlling its evolution?

310
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:33,780
Yes, sir.

311
00:15:34,200 --> 00:15:37,800
We must structure an evolution that leads to self-destruction, death itself.

312
00:15:38,060 --> 00:15:42,000
We'll set it up so that absorbing the Magi will lead to an evolutionary dead end.

313
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:47,700
If the Angels believe it to be their only practical means of survival, they may choose to co-exist with the Magi's system.

314
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:48,500
But how?

315
00:15:48,860 --> 00:15:49,720
What's your plan?

316
00:15:50,220 --> 00:15:54,680
Since this Angel is like a computer, we could hack into it by connecting it to Kaspar.

317
00:15:54,880 --> 00:15:58,800
Once we've done that, we could then upload some kind of auto-self-destruct program.

318
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:04,080
But in order to do that, we'll have to remove the barriers that are protecting the last Magi.

319
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:08,320
But if Kaspar is faster than the Angel, we'll succeed.

320
00:16:08,860 --> 00:16:09,220
Yes.

321
00:16:09,660 --> 00:16:11,860
This program, can it be ready in time?

322
00:16:12,220 --> 00:16:14,980
If Kaspar's taken over first, it'll be all over.

323
00:16:17,300 --> 00:16:19,020
I keep my promises.

324
00:16:19,640 --> 00:16:21,480
Red alert. Red alert.

325
00:16:21,940 --> 00:16:24,040
An emergency has occurred in Nerve headquarters.

326
00:16:24,520 --> 00:16:26,820
All T-class personnel must be died straight.

327
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:41,860
What are those paper things, ma'am?

328
00:16:49,220 --> 00:16:51,260
These are the developer's personal notes.

329
00:16:51,720 --> 00:16:53,680
My God, they're access codes.

330
00:16:53,900 --> 00:16:55,420
The Magi's secret codes.

331
00:16:55,680 --> 00:16:58,220
It's like having a map to all of the Magi's back doors.

332
00:16:58,760 --> 00:17:00,220
Am I allowed to see these?

333
00:17:00,420 --> 00:17:02,660
I can't believe this is all INTC.

334
00:17:03,460 --> 00:17:03,860
Schematics.

335
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:04,920
Everything.

336
00:17:05,740 --> 00:17:08,180
With these notes, we can program much faster than we thought.

337
00:17:08,440 --> 00:17:09,060
Right, ma'am?

338
00:17:10,180 --> 00:17:10,540
Mm-hmm.

339
00:17:12,060 --> 00:17:12,900
Thanks, Mom.

340
00:17:13,400 --> 00:17:14,860
With your help, we can make it.

341
00:17:22,860 --> 00:17:23,460
Mm-hmm.

342
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:26,080
Okay.

343
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:27,420
Rich, please.

344
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:33,300
Hey, doesn't this remind you of our college days?

345
00:17:33,300 --> 00:17:35,720
Board number 25, please.

346
00:17:41,140 --> 00:17:43,860
So, why don't you tell me all about the Magi?

347
00:17:44,520 --> 00:17:46,000
It's a long story.

348
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:52,180
Do you know about the personality transplant OS?

349
00:17:52,180 --> 00:17:52,740
Yeah.

350
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:59,220
It's a system for implanting personality onto a seventh-generation systematic computer to allow the system to think for itself.

351
00:17:59,220 --> 00:18:02,480
The same technology is used for operating the AAPS.

352
00:18:02,480 --> 00:18:06,060
The Magi's programming used one of the first test subjects.

353
00:18:06,060 --> 00:18:10,160
So, since my mother was the one who developed the technology...

354
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:14,980
You mean it was her personality that was transplanted?

355
00:18:14,980 --> 00:18:15,640
That's right.

356
00:18:15,640 --> 00:18:15,740
That's right.

357
00:18:25,740 --> 00:18:30,320
In a very real sense, the Magi's brains are my mother.

358
00:18:30,320 --> 00:18:33,480
Is that why you want to protect the Magi?

359
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:34,780
I don't think so.

360
00:18:35,080 --> 00:18:38,520
Actually, to be quite honest, I never really liked my mother.

361
00:18:38,740 --> 00:18:39,120
Oh.

362
00:18:39,120 --> 00:18:41,040
My decision was that of a scientist.

363
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:44,040
It's happening!

364
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:45,780
Balthazar is being taken over!

365
00:18:45,880 --> 00:18:49,140
Flash-Eye auto self-destruction sequence has been determined.

366
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:50,660
It started!

367
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:54,540
Self-destruction will occur 20 seconds after all three AI consent.

368
00:18:55,020 --> 00:19:03,520
Area of destruction will include geoid depth minus 280, minus 140, and floor 0.

369
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:06,900
Under special command 582...

370
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:08,560
Balthazar is now invading Caspar!

371
00:19:08,940 --> 00:19:09,960
They're faster than us.

372
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:10,740
They're faster...

373
00:19:10,740 --> 00:19:11,100
All right.

374
00:19:12,580 --> 00:19:13,020
But...

375
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:17,720
T minus 20 seconds to self-destruct.

376
00:19:18,240 --> 00:19:19,100
My God!

377
00:19:19,380 --> 00:19:21,560
Caspar will be taken over in 18 seconds!

378
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:24,560
T minus 15 seconds to self-destruct.

379
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:26,100
Weeds go, hurry!

380
00:19:26,400 --> 00:19:27,060
Don't worry.

381
00:19:27,380 --> 00:19:28,940
I've got one whole second to spare.

382
00:19:29,280 --> 00:19:30,300
Only one second?

383
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:32,140
That's not a zero or a minus.

384
00:19:32,140 --> 00:19:39,140
Seven, six, five, four, three, two, one, zero.

385
00:19:51,140 --> 00:19:53,900
Autonomous self-destruct has been cancelled.

386
00:19:55,500 --> 00:19:55,980
Yeah!

387
00:19:56,920 --> 00:20:00,480
Special command 582 is cancelled.

388
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:03,400
Mesh eye system returning to normal mode.

389
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:05,640
Red alert has been cancelled.

390
00:20:14,440 --> 00:20:16,260
Red alert has been cancelled.

391
00:20:16,820 --> 00:20:18,280
Red alert has been cancelled.

392
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:20,680
All hands return to first stage alert.

393
00:20:20,680 --> 00:20:22,100
Oh, what's going on out there?

394
00:20:22,100 --> 00:20:28,240
Oh, how am I going to get out of here naked?

395
00:20:29,360 --> 00:20:31,100
Somebody help me!

396
00:20:33,720 --> 00:20:35,500
Sigma unit has been released.

397
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:38,400
T minus 0-3 to magi reactivation.

398
00:20:39,860 --> 00:20:42,240
I must be getting old.

399
00:20:42,620 --> 00:20:44,420
These all-nighters are really rough.

400
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:46,500
Yeah, but at least you kept your promise again.

401
00:20:47,060 --> 00:20:47,860
You did good.

402
00:20:47,860 --> 00:20:49,340
Oh, thank you.

403
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:51,700
Mmm.

404
00:20:53,980 --> 00:20:58,740
You know, this is the first time I've ever really appreciated this paint thinner you call coffee.

405
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:01,500
The night before she died,

406
00:21:02,080 --> 00:21:05,140
my mother told me that the magi were the three aspects of her life.

407
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:06,700
Herself as a scientist,

408
00:21:07,280 --> 00:21:08,220
herself as a mother,

409
00:21:08,540 --> 00:21:09,480
and herself as a woman.

410
00:21:09,480 --> 00:21:13,600
Those three aspects of her are struggling for dominance inside the magi.

411
00:21:14,360 --> 00:21:17,700
She intentionally implanted the dilemmas of the human experience into it.

412
00:21:18,340 --> 00:21:18,740
Actually,

413
00:21:19,220 --> 00:21:21,620
each of the three programs are slightly different as well.

414
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:23,180
You know,

415
00:21:23,280 --> 00:21:26,560
I don't think I'm the kind of woman who will ever have children of my own,

416
00:21:26,900 --> 00:21:29,100
so I don't really understand her as a mother,

417
00:21:29,240 --> 00:21:31,020
but I respected her as a scientist.

418
00:21:31,740 --> 00:21:32,100
However,

419
00:21:32,200 --> 00:21:33,420
when it came to her as a woman,

420
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:34,280
I hated her.

421
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:36,560
Well,

422
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:38,320
you're rather talkative today.

423
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:40,080
About some things.

424
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:49,800
The program that was installed in Caspar was the one of my mother as a woman.

425
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:53,060
And she stayed a woman down to the very last second.

426
00:21:53,340 --> 00:21:54,680
How totally like my mother.

427
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:55,740
Phylologics.

428
00:21:55,740 --> 00:21:56,680
Phylologics.

429
00:21:57,120 --> 00:21:57,640
Phylologics.

430
00:22:16,060 --> 00:22:23,940
Bhay Ne positon.

431
00:22:23,940 --> 00:22:31,740
In other words, darling, kiss me.

432
00:22:33,260 --> 00:22:40,080
Fill my heart with song, outlet me sing forevermore.

433
00:22:41,620 --> 00:22:48,240
You are all I love, for all I wish you'd end the door.

434
00:22:48,240 --> 00:22:57,160
In other words, please speak to you.

435
00:22:57,160 --> 00:23:04,160
In other words, I love, I love you.

436
00:23:18,240 --> 00:23:19,560
Will the answers be revealed?

